\newlabel{fig:latent}{{2}{5}{Step-size policies improve fixed-depth exact match at constant compute. Inner-subset EM gain (pp) over the original $\alpha {\approx }1$ update for random search and three evolutionary optimizers at equal budgets of 336 evaluations. Feature-group ablations on $s_0$ show that the time index alone and the dynamics pair alone each reproduce the full-feature gain, while entropy alone does not}{figure.caption.9}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Refinement steps change the latent state less as depth grows. Per-step displacement and direction consistency of the latent trajectory under fixed damping on the frozen GRU decoder. The concentration of small displacements at later steps motivates a step-size policy that reads entropy, displacement, and direction consistency at decision time.}}{5}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:traj}{{3}{5}{Refinement steps change the latent state less as depth grows. Per-step displacement and direction consistency of the latent trajectory under fixed damping on the frozen GRU decoder. The concentration of small displacements at later steps motivates a step-size policy that reads entropy, displacement, and direction consistency at decision time}{figure.caption.10}{}}
